hat?", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\n•", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\nThe more open, challenging questions came towards the end using command words\nsuch as  explain, suggest, comment on and justify.", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\n•", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\nAs in previous years,  the team also tried to produce sections that integrated physical and human geography topics.", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\n•", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\nWe always try to provide a variety of data representation/visualisation (eg. maps,\ngraphs, tables, etc.) to reflect the range of sources that geographers work with.", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\n•", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\nWe also tried to introduce some more modern topics e.g. geography of health; the\nsolar powered boat schools and the recent expansion of globalisation.", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\n•", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\nSome questions were very poorly answered by students:", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\no", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\nIn question C7 students were asked to comment on the differences between\nthe data shown in the table for Africa and Oceania.  87 students did not\nscore on this part.", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\no", _jsx(_components.br, {}), "\nQuestionA4 asked students to draw a series of diagrams to show the formation of a delta.  58 students did not score on this part.62 students were unable to give a reasonable definition of globalisation in question F1."]
